---
TDL: 0.2
Shell: 0.1
Name: List
---

# A scrolling list (Standard Modules > List): its entries are the call's children, usually a `For`
# keyed by an id. The wheel scrolls it (it is 240 by 200 pixels unless the call writes a `Width` or
# a `Height`). An entry has a key (a `For` entry the repeater's key, any other writes `Key: name`);
# a click chooses it: `Selection: SINGLE` (the default) takes the click, `NONE` ignores it and
# `MULTIPLE` chooses a set the way the Selection pattern says (the engine's own container selection:
# click, Shift+click a range, Ctrl+click a toggle, Shift+Up and Down extend, Ctrl+Up and Down move
# the focus, Ctrl+Space toggles, Ctrl+A chooses all, a disabled entry is skipped, Escape keeps the
# set; it is multiselectable for assistive technology and announces "N selected" once). Then
# `Selected` and `On_Changed`'s `old`, `new` and `value` are the keys of the chosen entries joined
# by a comma (a key has no comma), in the order of the entries; the type-ahead search is SINGLE's.
# `Selected` is the chosen entry's key, set from outside (it marks the entry and raises nothing);
# `On_Changed` fires when the user chooses one (`event.old`, `event.new` and `event.value` are the
# keys). The chosen entry takes the style state `:selected` (and the role OPTION carries
# `selected`), so give the entries a class and style `.list_item:selected`; the Default stylesheet
# does for the class `list_item`. The role is LISTBOX, and OPTION for the entries, when the List
# can be chosen from (`SINGLE`, `MULTIPLE`; MULTIPLE is multiselectable); LIST when `Selection: NONE`
# (AC-LST-01).
# Keys: the List is one Tab stop and its entries are reached with the arrow keys. Up and Down move
# the chosen entry (the first Down chooses the first entry, the first Up the last), Page Up and
# Page Down by a page, Home and End to the ends, Enter and Space choose the first entry when none
# is chosen, and letters typed jump to the next entry whose text starts with them (a space in a
# search is a letter of it; the search ends a second after the last letter). Each move is a choice:
# `On_Changed` fires and the entry scrolls into view. A disabled entry is passed over, a List with
# `Selection: NONE` takes no key, and a focused List keeps the keys, so they do not scroll a
# ScrollBox around it.
# `Empty` is the text the List shows when it has no entries and `Count` is 0: the caller passes the
# number of entries it loops over (a module cannot count its Content), so `Count` is -1, unknown,
# unless written. The empty text is one node inside the List, which keeps its role and name
# (Empty States).
#   List { Selected: <| picked |>, On_Changed: choose, Children { For ... Key <| w.id |> { ... } } }
#   List { Empty: "No results", Count: <| results_count |>, Children { For ... } }
Module {
    Params {
        Selected { Type: string, Default: "" }
        Selection { Type: string, Default: SINGLE }
        Label { Type: string, Default: "" }
        Empty { Type: string, Default: "" }
        Count { Type: number, Default: -1 }
    }
    ScrollBox {
        Name: Root
        Role: <| "LIST" if params.Selection == "NONE" else "LISTBOX" |>
        Label: <| params.Label |>
        Selection_Mode: <| params.Selection |>
        Chosen: <| params.Selected |>
        Width: 240
        Height: 200
        Children {
            FlexBox {
                Name: Items
                Flex: VERTICAL
                Align_Items: STRETCH
                Children {
                    If <| params.Empty != "" and params.Count == 0 |> {
                        Text {
                            Name: Empty
                            Foreground: $color.on_surface_muted
                            Text: <| params.Empty |>
                            Wrap: NONE
                            Width: AUTO
                            Height: AUTO
                            Padding: <| [density.row_padding_x, 8, density.row_padding_x, 8] |>
                        }
                    }
                    Content { }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
